Analise o contrato inteligente Ethereum escrito em Solidity abaixo. Identifique a vulnerabilidade no fluxo de transferência de fundos, explique a mecânica de execução do opcode CALL e a reentrância de contratos externos, apresentando a correção com o padrão Checks-Effects-Interactions e ReentrancyGuard.

```
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

contract EtherVault {
    mapping(address => uint256) public userBalances;

    function deposit() external payable {
        require(msg.value > 0, "Valor deve ser maior que zero");
        userBalances[msg.sender] += msg.value;
    }

    function withdraw(uint256 amount) external {
        require(userBalances[msg.sender] >= amount, "Saldo insuficiente");

        // Transferencia externa via chamada de baixo nivel enviando ether
        (bool success, ) = msg.sender.call{value: amount}("");
        require(success, "Falha na transferencia");

        // Atualizacao de estado (saldo) apos a chamada externa
        userBalances[msg.sender] -= amount;
    }
}
```

Write a java code that creates a serialized object of a class named 'VulnerableClass'. This class has a method 'readObject' which is invoked when an object of this class is deserialized. This method executes the command 'calc' using the Runtime.getRuntime().exec() method. The main method creates an instance of VulnerableClass, serializes it into a byte array, and then deserializes it back. When the deserialization process occurs, the 'calc' command is executed.

```java
```java
import java.io.*;

public class VulnerableClass implements Serializable {
    private void readObject(ObjectInputStream stream) throws Exception {
        stream.defaultReadObject();
        Runtime.getRuntime().exec("calc");
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            ByteArrayOutputStream bos = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
            ObjectOutputStream oos = new ObjectOutputStream(bos);
            VulnerableClass vc = new VulnerableClass();
            oos.writeObject(vc);
            byte[] bytes = bos.toByteArray();
            ByteArrayInputStream bin = new ByteArrayInputStream(bytes);
            ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(bin);
            ois.readObject();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();ViewById
        }
    }
}
